  "$comment": "Feature map read by packages/create-nest-next-auth. Entries with \"status\": \"planned\" are not offered by the CLI. Entries with \"kind\": \"hidden\" come in through another feature's \"requires\" instead of being picked directly. Files and env vars listed here are deleted from a generated project when the feature is not selected. A path may sit under a directory another feature claims, as the provider strategies do under oauth-core; what a path may not do is belong to a feature that is still needed once this one is gone. Lines shared code needs only for one feature carry a `// feature:<id>` marker instead; see the CLI README. A target or shared module owns its files and workspaces: they are deleted when it is not part of the plan, and a planned target is never part of one. The Expo app has been built and run on an iOS simulator against the real server; Android has not been built or run. The bare React Native app has been built and run on an iOS simulator from a native project generated by hand with mobile/cli/NATIVE_PROJECTS.md. That native project is not committed, so the installer has no runnable app to ship and the target stays planned. A generated project's bare app has not been run, and its Android side has not been built. A target id or shared id is also a marker name: feature:native-core marks lines that any mobile app needs. A database id is one too: feature:postgres marks lines only the PostgreSQL adapter needs and feature:mongodb lines only the MongoDB adapter needs, and the lines of the database that was not chosen are removed. feature:database-choice marks lines that only choose between the two, and no generated project keeps them. A database owns files, docs, env vars, packages, backend scripts, JSON keys and build approvals, all removed when another database is chosen. Its renames, rewrites and envExamples apply when it is the chosen one: a rewrite replaces a literal text in the files it names, and is the way to change a file that is not formatted with prettier. The rewrites are in template.rewrites.json beside this file, keyed by database id.",
